# DURABLE REPRO — D10 exclusivity hole A7: the WRITER is nested ONE CALL DEEP
# inside a sibling argument.
#
# `f(v[0], mutate(&v))` — arg 0 is a live element borrow, arg 1 is an
# expression that *contains* `&v`. The overlap check only looks at the top-level
# shape of each argument, so a writer one syntactic level down is invisible.
#
# WRONG TODAY (measured at HEAD, Rust gg, C backend, `--sanitize`): `gg check`
# clean, then AddressSanitizer heap-use-after-free in `gorget_string_copy_cow`.
# Left-to-right evaluation reads `v[0]` into a borrow, `mutate(&v)` reallocs,
# and the callee then copies from the dangling element.
#
# INTENDED: REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_BorrowConflict`. A writer anywhere
# inside a sibling argument's expression tree is a participant.
#
# The 4096-push loop FORCES a real reallocation.
#
#
# ORACLE (ggdef, measured this session): ACCEPTS this program and prints the
# pre-mutation value. ggdef is a definitional INTERPRETER with value semantics,
# so a reallocation cannot invalidate anything and this UAF class is
# structurally unobservable in that lane — it is NOT the authority here. The
# intended REJECT comes from the ratified D10 exclusivity ruling, which ggdef
# owes as part of the same landing (Core #9). Full note in
# `sound_excl_getchain_local.gg`.
# Cited from TODO.md (CoW / ownership / High): the D10 "one exclusive writer"
# structural-chokepoint entry (nested-writer costume).
int mutate(Vector[String] &v):
    int i = 0
    while i < 4096:
        v.push("filler-padding-to-force-a-real-reallocation")
        i = i + 1
    return v.len()

void f(String s, int n):
    print(s)
    print(n)

void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("alpha-heap-forced-payload")
    f(v[0], mutate(&v))
